 # records
 
 Small text-record helpers. Run the tests with `npm test` (node:test).
+
+`parseRecords(text)` from `src/records.js` parses one record per non-blank
+line. Fields are separated by semicolons and use `key=value`; keys begin with
+a lowercase letter and contain only lowercase letters, digits, and underscores.
+Values are trimmed and may contain `=`. Invalid or duplicate keys and fields
+without `=` throw `SyntaxError` with the 1-based line number. Non-string input
+throws `TypeError`.
+
+`select(records, field, value)` returns matching records in input order using
+strict equality. It throws `TypeError` if `records` is not an array.
